WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.690
We'll change.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.150
We'll win and prove it to them!

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.320
That's right, we can do it!

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.740
The game is slowly turning in our favor!

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.810
Like I said, I'm just going out for a while!

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.570
Even so, you'll always end up drinking with Shige after the match!

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.450
Y-You're wrong! I'm just...

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.360
What's with that outfit, then?

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.700
It's already the second half!

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.580
I'm going out for a bit!

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.290
H-Hold on! Stop right there, you stupid husband!

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:37.090
There's no way I'm missing this!

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.630
It's Tatsumi's opening match today!

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.940
During the match against Tokyo Victory, Tatsumi was only giving instructions in the technical area.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.860
It's just like ten years ago!

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.400
I'm so excited!

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.820
Tatsumi's amazing! He's still able to show us such exciting stuff as a manager!

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:03.870
With him at the helm,

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.080
ETU may just be able to win the league!

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.490
Goal! It's the fourth one!

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.590
What's this? They're being ripped apart.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.720
They started off well, but crumbled and faded away as the game wore on.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.650
The first goal.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.580
Right after the first goal, ETU's formation went into a mess, just like a broken chain.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:36.960
Get to the goal now! Hurry!

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.340
Stop your aimless running, Tsubaki! Calm down!

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.130
Hurry up and get back into position! Do you even intend to defend at all?

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:51.680
Why? That initial goal was just a complete fluke. It shouldn't have affected them much, right?

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:56.940
Is it really alright for me to follow up on such a team?

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.670
They look so down that I don't even know how to comfort them.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.380
The cracks are showing up on your new team, Tatsumi...

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.140
We've lost.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.310
It was a pity.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:39.900
I'm gutted.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:41.770
That is all.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.120
As I expected, he's not worth listening to at all.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.660
You can now start asking questions.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.550
The female reporter over there.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:04.380
Thanks.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:06.880
I'm Fujisawa, a freelance writer.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:13.810
During the conference, you mentioned about transforming the Japanese league into an exciting one.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:20.940
I believe that a lot of people were encouraged by your words.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.320
However,

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:29.530
The performance today betrayed those who believe in what you said.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:33.030
Miss Fujisawa sure isn't mincing her words.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.660
Are you still expecting these people to harbor that hope?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.840
Well, what?

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.210
Are you angry?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.590
I'm not, please answer my question!

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.060
So you <i>are</i> angry.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:55.970
I said I'm not!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.730
But your expression doesn't indicate so!

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.100
What are you talking about?

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.600
You're rude!

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:01.900
Am I?
What should I do?

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:02.100
What should I do?

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:14.080
What's with this guy? I've had enough! I'm not gonna bet my whole year on him!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.700
There's still time. I can still request for a change of clubs!

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:17.410
You can.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.170
You guys can continue to believe in me.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.520
Tsubaki, hurry up and catch up!

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.270
We won't win if we can't score!

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:44.690
You're running way ahead, Tsubaki!

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:45.940
You turd!

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.650
We're finished if we concede another!

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.900
Catch up, Tsubaki!

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.120
I told you to come back, Tsubaki!

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.410
How many times do I need to tell you guys?! The space!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.040
There's way too much space in midfield!

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.380
Are you all really putting in effort?!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.300
We'll lose if we carry on like this, you hear me?!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.470
He was still confidently telling me to believe in him... What the hell are they doing?

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.310
And I took such a long trip to Hiroshima.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.650
We lost again.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.450
Two consecutive league losses...

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.430
What in the world happened?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.310
We did learn from our mistakes from the opening loss and improve...

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:09.690
That's two straight losses, and we haven't even scored a single goal. It's a real headache.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.860
Who's that laughing just now?!

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.150
I heard that!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:18.160
We've already lost twice in a row, and yet you're still laughing.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:24.580
We need to come together to raise morale in this kind of situation!

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:26.540
Here...

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:27.960
...we go again.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.710
The one laughing just now must be Gino.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.800
Forget it.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.180
Everyone's tired.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.350
What's that, Akasaki?

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.850
The one not defending during the match dares to say that he's tired.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:50.690
Thanks to you guys storming forward, the opponent made use of the space in midfield.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:53.400
You guys have to use your brains before you act, dumbass!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.610
What are you saying?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:00.410
It's because you're too afraid of your opponents that you sit way too deep!

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.580
I am definitely giving my all.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.250
You should reflect on your own performance before criticizing others!

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.340
In truth, we've conceded way too many.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.760
Don't screw with me, you bastard!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:16.130
Ouch!

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.510
Crap, it started!

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.430
Stop it, Kuro!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.970
We only did that to maintain the balance of the team!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:25.980
What?

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.520
Don't give me that know-it-all face!

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.190
Murakoshi, is this alright?

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.230
Leave them be...

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:42.370
If they can still quarrel after a match, it means we've lost a game that we were destined to lose.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.290
Let me go, Sugi!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:51.420
He's also looking down on you! Do you intend to let him continue his wayward thinking?

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.460
This is not the place to fight, Kuro.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:59.340
It'll be a mess if we let this happen again during tomorrow's training.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:11.940
What happened, Tsubaki?

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:17.440
You better get your act up. You're useless in both attack and defense.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.150
You're really trash!

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.260
This doesn't look good, manager!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.010
If the team morale were to get any worse...

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.220
Macchan...

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.050
Yes?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.270
What kind of games do you like?

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:59.150
W-What are you talking about?

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.450
This is an important question.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.950
Let's see...

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:10.160
If I have to pick one, I would say it's Shogi.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.160
Just as I expected, it's that!

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.000
Let's play that then.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.800
Manager, are you okay?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.050
The squad is already a mess, but...

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.470
I'm so worried. Very worried.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:44.450
Gotou...

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.200
Tatsumi.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.620
I have lots of faith in you.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.920
Hey, I have a question for you.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:01.920
How many more games can I lose before I get the sack?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.960
Stop screwing around with me.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.090
That asshole!

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:48.140
Why did we have to be dropped to the bench?

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:52.140
All because of the outcome of some kids game!

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.980
What? A game competition?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:00.480
Right.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:05.900
And so, let's have my assistant, Macchan, to explain the details.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:07.950
Y-Yes.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:14.450
The game will be 'Soccer-Tennis'. You'll pair up in twos to play.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.370
The pair with the highest score will be awarded with a fabulous prize.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.500
Put some enthusiasm in your instructions!

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:22.670
Yes.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:29.550
For your partner, you are to pair up with a player of the same position.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.350
Therefore, everyone...

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:33.720
Aim for first place!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:37.310
Aye, aye, ooo...

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:44.190
Man, you wasted such a cool line!

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.610
I put in so much effort to write this.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.070
Let's start then!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:51.070
Form your teams now!

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:54.660
Oi, Manager!

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:00.540
We don't need time for a rest to play a few games...

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.670
We have to concentrate on working hard in training!

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.510
You were once a player yourself,

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.880
You should know what it feels like to lose two consecutive matches!

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:14.010
Alright, let's practice!

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:21.100
But I did play that kind of games too during my player days...

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.270
G-Game?

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:29.320
How can you still say that with a straight face? So it's still a game!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:33.030
Didn't I just say it's a game competition?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:39.290
Quit joking around! The third match's coming soon and there is no time for games!

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:45.790
We're different from the lame team you managed back in England!

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:52.970
Are we playing this in order to win?

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:04.310
Of course.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:09.820
Tsubaki.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.900
Y-Yes?

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:13.110
Team up with me.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.990
Don't we need to pair up with a player of the same position?

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.910
Since Murakoshi wants to play, why don't we...

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:20.750
Yeah.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.460
Then we side-backs should team up.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.850
Alright! We've leveled!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:47.480
Amazing! Keep it up!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.650
Dori, that's a great move!

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.490
It's as if you can play as a striker too, Dori!

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:02.160
Alright, 20-0. We've lost.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:07.000
It's over! Who would play this kind of boring game?

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.050
You shouldn't be doing this, Kuro.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.220
After all, it's still something devised by the manager.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.680
It's better to heed his advice.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.800
He said it's just a game himself!

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.430
That's not the point.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:26.310
I will only make the effort if it concerns winning a game.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.480
Hey Tatsumi, do you have any collection of your interest?

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.280
I have a bit of an interest in chairs lately.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.700
Therefore if I win, please give me a comfy chair as a prize.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:38.660
Not possible.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:44.290
Is that so? Well, the chair that I fancy does cost two million yen.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:45.960
The fabulous prize is...

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.090
A starting place for the next game!

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.270
The first goal of the season!

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.560
Yes!

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.600
Great! Nice goal, Sera!

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.020
Akasaki's assist is nice too!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:19.200
No matter how much more we throw at them, it's still not enough!

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:25.500
Kobayashi and Kame ain't that bad of a player too.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.210
I have to look over my shoulders now...

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.000
That bastard.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:36.970
If he had put us on for the second half, we might have been able to get a narrow win.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:42.050
What's the matter, Sugi?

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.180
Oh, nothing.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:49.230
Look. It's gonna end. Serves him right.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.660
We lost again.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.620
We've lost three in a row!

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.080
This is really...

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.920
...pushing our patience to the limit.

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:18.510
I've decided, Sugi.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:23.970
I need to transfer clubs! I'm not playing under him anymore!

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.320
A transfer? Kuroda?

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:50.040
Though I think he's just saying it in the heat of the moment.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:55.840
But I would want to hear your opinion, Dori.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:59.300
That's a rare occurrence, Sugi.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:03.430
Isn't this a matter you would normally ask Murakoshi?

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:06.930
Yeah, but...

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:08.810
Recently, Murakoshi has...

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.560
...been giving off a sense of unapproachability.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.520
It's like he has become a lone wolf.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:19.570
That's true.

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:23.990
However, he is a man with a strong sense of responsibility.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.080
He has his own set of opinions too.

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.120
I feel the same for Tatsumi too.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:36.210
He also has his way of thinking.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.340
Using that kind of game to determine the starting line-up.

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:44.510
It's not only Kuroda that's feeling a sense of exhalation.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:50.600
If that's a game, then he has his own reasons for using it to plot his course of action.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.230
I feel that Tatsumi is that kind of a person.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.520
Though it's only my feelings.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:04.780
Before letting Kuroda decide on whether to change clubs, make sure that he's putting himself in other people's shoes.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:09.370
Dori...

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:14.330
I still have something to ask you.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.840
What should I do?

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:24.760
Should I tell the manager?

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:29.180
But Kuroda handed in a transfer request,

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.850
That's obviously showing a sign of dissatisfaction towards the manager.

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:41.190
I'll just try to mediate here...

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:44.280
Well,

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:47.990
We will now also conduct a competition to determine the starting line-up.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.160
Again?

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:57.540
It's not gonna work, manager! That was the reason why we lost the previous game!

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:02.750
It was because of Tsubaki's failings that Murakoshi had to be subbed off so early in the match!

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:06.050
That was only a reference.

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:08.340
The end product is not everything.

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:11.930
But in truth, Kuroda and Sugi have...

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.850
That's about all I can take...

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:17.100
Kuro!

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:18.980
Hey, Kuro!

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:21.400
This is bad.

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:25.440
It's no joke. Things really are turning for the worse.

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:35.200
Those who don't feel like playing the next match are allowed to not participate.

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:39.960
However, those who want to win the next game...

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:43.500
Go ahead and enjoy the competition!

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:17.560
The person that we have to defeat...

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:18.970
...is ourselves.

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:20.480
We didn't change.

00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:22.770
We've only thought that we changed.

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:23.980
Damn it!

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:26.230
To have their places taken away by the youngsters...

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:28.230
It should be about time...
